{
  "id": "BankBalanceC01",
  "slug": "bank-balance/c01",
  "chapter": "Cold open",
  "topic": "What if you could see everyone's bank balance?",
  "script": [
    {
      "beat": "the postman",
      "text": "You wake up and look out of the window. The postman is walking up the path, and there's a number floating above his head. Eight hundred and forty dollars and twelve cents. Green. He turns around. The number turns with him."
    },
    {
      "beat": "the bus",
      "text": "On the bus, everyone has one. The driver: three hundred and eight dollars. A woman with a gold watch and a designer bag: minus sixty-one thousand. Red. A kid your age with big headphones: nine thousand. Birthday money he has never touched."
    },
    {
      "beat": "the hoodie",
      "text": "A guy in a hoodie, eating crisps out of the bag: four point two million."
    },
    {
      "beat": "jake and mo",
      "text": "At school, Jake, who never stops talking about his dad's boat, is at eleven dollars. Mo, your best friend, is at three dollars and twelve cents. He buys a chocolate bar. Now it's one sixty-two."
    },
    {
      "beat": "premise question",
      "text": "Every person. Every account. To the cent. Live. And nobody else can see them. Just you. So what would actually happen if you could see everyone's bank balance?"
    }
  ],
